# Local edits, cloud via sync

- Make every code and content change in the local workspace first
- Do not SSH, scp, rsync, restart, or otherwise modify the cloud host
- Do not treat a remote deploy or a remote process restart as part of the change
- The cloud copy, including http://134.175.139.38:8000, is updated by the existing sync method
- Reading the cloud page to inspect behavior is fine; writing to it is not

## Examples

```text
BAD: edit files on the server, or restart uvicorn on 134.175.139.38
GOOD: edit the local repo, run local checks, leave the cloud update to sync
```
